  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chain-join-border"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "chain-join border"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " converts the outer round of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble clusters"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " into a row of chain-3 loops, each anchored to the top of a cluster from the previous round with a slip stitch. The border serves two purposes: it gives a lighter, lacier edge than a standard cluster round, and the chain-3 loops become joining points when assembling multiple squares — replacing the joining slip stitch into a cluster top (which can pull and distort) with a slip stitch into a chain space (which sits flat). Start from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " opens the chain loops so they sit evenly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 30 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "10 × 10 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. The chain border adds slight openness at the edge — if the loops are too loose, go down to a 3.5 mm hook for round 4 only."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double crochet (dc) — UK"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 at the start of rounds 1 to 3 counts as the first tr. Round 4 is the chain border — no ch 3 turning chain."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr, ch 2. *(3 tr, ch 2); repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. Pull tail. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in ch-1 sp on side. Ch 1. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. 3 tr in last side sp. Ch 1. Sl st to top of ch-3. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 8 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4 — chain-join border"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 1 (does not count as a st). *1 dc into top of next cluster. Ch 3. Sl st into the same cluster top (loop anchored). Repeat from * into each cluster top and each ch-1 side space around all four sides, working (1 dc, ch 5, 1 dc) into each ch-2 corner space for a wider corner loop. Sl st to first dc to join. Fasten off. (12 chain-3 loops on sides, 4 chain-5 corner loops)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet-block to 10 × 10 cm, pinning through the chain loops to hold them open. The chain-3 loops need pinning to sit evenly — they will bunch without blocking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To join two squares with the chain border, place them right sides together. Replace the ch-3 loops on the joining edge with: ch 1, sl st into corresponding chain-3 loop of adjacent square, ch 1 (joined loop). At each joining corner, insert through both corner loops. This method keeps the border looking identical on both squares while lying flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. Reshape while damp and dry flat. Re-pin the chain loops if they close during washing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the chain border in a contrast colour — join a contrast yarn at the start of round 4. Or extend the chain length from 3 to 5 chains per loop for a more pronounced lace effect on the border."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}